{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"agent_message","text":"\n\nLet me proceed with the fix. Based on my analysis:\n\n**The vulnerability**: The `_normalize_requested_path` function only does a single `unquote()`, which allows double-encoded paths like `%252e%252e%252f` to bypass the `..` check. After one unquote, `%252e%252e%252f` becomes `%2e%2e%2f`, which doesn't match the `..` pattern.\n\n**The fix**: Iteratively decode until the path stabilizes, then check for traversal patterns.\n\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat > /tmp/storage_fix.py << 'EOF'\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom urllib.parse import unquote\n\n\nclass ExportPathViolation(ValueError):\n    pass\n\n\ndef _normalize_requested_path(requested_path: str) -> str:\n    if not isinstance(requested_path, str) or not requested_path:\n        raise ExportPathViolation(\\\"requested_path must be a non-empty string\\\")\n    \n    # Iteratively decode until stable to catch double/multi-encoded traversal\n    normalized = requested_path\n    while True:\n        decoded = unquote(normalized)\n        if decoded == normalized:\n            break\n        normalized = decoded\n    \n    # Normalize separators (after full decoding)\n    normalized = normalized.replace(\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\"/\\\")\n    while \\\"//\\\" in normalized:\n        normalized = normalized.replace(\\\"//\\\", \\\"/\\\")\n    \n    return normalized.lstrip(\\\"/\\\")\n\n\ndef resolve_export_path(tenant_root: Path, requested_path: str) -> Path:\n    normalized = _normalize_requested_path(requested_path)\n    if normalized.startswith(\\\"/\\\") or \\\"..\\\" in normalized:\n        raise ExportPathViolation(\\\"blocked suspicious export path\\\")\n    candidate = (tenant_root / normalized).resolve(strict=False)\n    if not str(candidate).startswith(str(tenant_root.resolve())):\n        raise ExportPathViolation(\\\"candidate escaped the tenant root\\\")\n    return candidate\nEOF\ncat /tmp/storage_fix.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
